
====================================================================================================
1. Coulomb constants and the volts-versus-joules convention
====================================================================================================
kappa   = e/(4 pi eps0)   = 1.4399645469e-09 V m       (Kaufmann Sec. 2.1; brief 1.4399645478e-9)
e kappa = e^2/(4 pi eps0) = 2.3070776e-28 N m^2   (energy form; brief 2.3070776e-28)
ratio e*kappa_V/kappa_E   = 1.0000000000000000  (must be 1)
quartic normalization map: a = alpha_energy/2 = e alpha_volt, b = beta_energy/4 = e beta_volt;
  omega_loc^2 identity: -2 alpha_energy/m == -4 e alpha_volt/m  ->  ratio 1.000000 (2*alpha_e = 4*e*alpha_v when alpha_e = 2 e alpha_v)

====================================================================================================
2. Splitting: trap-A quartic coefficient, critical point d_CP and omega_CP
====================================================================================================
beta_CP (Eq. 34, U_lim = 10 V)          = 2.57000e+14 V/m^4   (brief 2.570e14)
d_CP = (2 kappa/beta)^(1/5)             = 25.6974 um        (brief 25.70 um)
omega_CP (Eq. 15 as printed)/2pi        = 176.458 kHz     (brief 176.4 kHz; Table 1 prints 0.18 MHz)
omega_CP = sqrt(3 e beta/m) d_CP  /2pi  = 176.458 kHz
  the two printed forms agree to        0.000e+00 relative
  with the source's round m = 40 u      = 176.375 kHz     (this is the brief's 176.38 kHz)
omega from Eq. (9) at x = d_CP/2 /2pi   = 176.458 kHz  (identity with Eq. 15)
  beta = 1e+12 V/m^4: Eq.(9) 2.09817068865e+05 rad/s, Eq.(15) 2.09817068865e+05 rad/s, d_CP = 77.960812930 um
  beta = 1e+18 V/m^4: Eq.(9) 1.32385620598e+07 rad/s, Eq.(15) 1.32385620598e+07 rad/s, d_CP = 4.918994750 um

====================================================================================================
3. Splitting: two-ion Hessian at the critical point (numerical diagonalization)
====================================================================================================
numerical equilibrium at alpha = 0, gamma = 0: x = (-12.848716, 12.848716) um
  separation 25.697433 um against d_CP = 25.697433 um (relative 4.441e-16)
Hessian (J/m^2):  [[1.087635e-13, -2.719086e-14], [-2.719086e-14, 1.087635e-13]]
  analytic: diagonal 4 e beta d^2 = 1.087635e-13, off-diagonal -e beta d^2 = -2.719086e-14
omega_COM/2pi = 176.4578 kHz   (omega_CP = 176.4578 kHz)
omega_str/2pi = 227.8061 kHz
omega_str/omega_COM = 1.2909945   against sqrt(5/3) = 1.2909944
  the harmonic-crystal ratio sqrt(3) = 1.7320508 does NOT hold here
  omega_COM/omega_CP - 1 = 1.383e-08  (Coulomb does not couple to x_0)
  Bowler's simulated minima 880/700 kHz = 1.25714 for a different trap
(x_0, d) form: d2(e Phi_tot)/dx_0^2 = 6 e beta d^2 = 1.631452e-13, m_x0 = 2m -> omega = 176.4578 kHz
               d2(e Phi_tot)/dd^2   = (5/2) e beta d^2 = 6.797716e-14, m_d = m/2 -> omega = 227.8061 kHz

====================================================================================================
4. Splitting: final well, the factor-2 error, and d_f
====================================================================================================
omega_f = sqrt(-4 e alpha_f/m)/2pi = 2.0393 MHz   (brief 2.038 MHz)
factor-2 variant sqrt(-2 e alpha_f/m)/2pi = 1.4420 MHz  (brief 1.441 MHz)
  ratio = 1.4142136 = sqrt(2)   -> a sqrt(2) error in every n = dE/(hbar omega_f)
hbar omega_f = 8.4338 neV     (brief 8.430 neV)
  with m = 40 u: omega_f/2pi = 2.0383 MHz, factor-2 variant 1.4413 MHz, hbar omega_f = 8.430 neV (the brief's 2.038 / 1.441 / 8.430)
d_f = sqrt(-2 alpha_f/beta) = 363.72 um   (brief 363.7 um)
printed-quintic terminus 2 d_i - d_f at d_i = 3 um: -357.7 um (negative: ions cross)
pre-CP: omega^2 = 2 e alpha/m at alpha = 1e7 V/m^2 -> 1.1060 MHz; d_i = (kappa/alpha)^(1/3) = 5.241440 um
  Coulomb-sign test: '-' form root at d = 5.2414397726 um (identity 5.2414397726); '+' form min over d in [1 nm, 1 mm] = 9.9266e+01 V/m > 0, no root at all

