  -> n_bar = 2.028e+04 against hbar omega_f, 2.344e+05 against hbar omega_CP
printed-chain coefficient pi^2/32 = 0.308425 versus printed Eq.(25) pi^2/8 = 1.233701, ratio 0.2500
x_0/gamma leading coeff printed = -1.964111567e-06 m per (V/m);  identity -1/(3 beta d_CP^2) = -1.964111567e-06
quadratic/linear ratio of Eq.(16) at |alpha| = 0.1 beta d_CP^2: 0.040000  (exactly 0.040 -> LINEAR-dominated)
the two smallness conditions: kappa d_CP^-3 = 8.48560e+04, beta d_CP^2/2 = 8.48560e+04 V/m^2 (equal)

====================================================================================================
6. Splitting: critical-tilt bifurcation, well depth and the voltage tolerance
====================================================================================================
V/s in reduced coordinate u: u*(u**3 - 3*u/2 + 1)
dV/du = (u + 1)*(2*u - 1)**2   (roots: double at u = 1/2, simple at u = -1)
V(saddle)/s = 3/16, V(minimum)/s = -3/2, depth = 27/16 = 1.687500
  27/16 = 1.687500; the printed subtraction order gives -1.687500
equal-value quartic factorizes as -(u - 2*xx)**3*(3*u + 2*xx)  -> x_tilde_c^(+) = -(3/2)(gamma/beta)^(1/3)
gamma_tilde = 1.06 (kappa^3 beta_CP^2)^(1/5) = 3.0499 V/m   (brief 3.050; paper ~3 V/m)
Delta U_O tolerance = gamma_tilde/gamma_O   = 9.53 mV     (brief 9.53; paper ~9 mV)
the paper's own saddle-balance heuristic gives C_gamma = (8/27)^(3/5) = 0.48199, a factor 2.199 smaller
tilt at which one ion's CP curvature doubles: 0.787 (kappa^3 beta^2)^(1/5) = 2.2644 V/m = 0.7425 gamma_tilde (74%, NOT the source's ~67%)
gamma_tilde scaling: proportional to beta_CP^(2/5), so the TOLERANCE grows with U_lim^(2/5) (x1.904 at U_lim = 50 V)

