15. Heating: the single-sided S_E round trip shared by splitting, transport and junctions
====================================================================================================
S_E = 4 m hbar omega_z ndot/q^2, 9Be+ at 3.6 MHz, 40 quanta/s = 2.2250e-13 (V/m)^2/Hz
  paper states 2.2e-13 at a 160 um ion-electrode distance; agreement 1.1%
back-substitution Gamma_h = e^2 S_E/(4 m hbar omega) = 40.0000 quanta/s
  40Ca+ at 2.5 MHz, 295 quanta/s (Sterk): S_E = 5.053e-12 (V/m)^2/Hz
  171Yb+ at 0.97 MHz, 300 quanta/s (Pino): S_E = 8.528e-12 (V/m)^2/Hz
anomalous heating over a 350 us E-C-E round trip at 40 quanta/s: 0.0140 quanta (paper says ~0.007; the factor ~2 is consistent with omega_z ramping to 5.7 MHz)
ambient heating over Sterk's 24 us round trip at 295 s^-1: 0.00708 quanta (paper: ~0.01)
one quantum at 3.6 MHz = 14.888 neV, so 0.1 quantum = 1.489 neV (the Table I caption's 1.6 neV is +7% off)

