  E-C-E     : 1.76 mm in 330 us -> 5.33 m/s, 158.4 updates, 11.1 um per update
  E-C-F-C-E : 3.52 mm in 890 us -> 3.96 m/s, 427.2 updates, 8.2 um per update
  E-C-V-C-E : 2.84 mm in 930 us -> 3.05 m/s, 446.4 updates, 6.4 um per update
  the 5 um figure is the BEM/solution grid spacing; a 5 um/update rule would pin v at 2.4 m/s
  and predict 733 us for the 330 us E-C-E move

====================================================================================================
21. Adiabaticity parameters (all three require ANGULAR frequencies)
====================================================================================================
Bowler's ramp caps: max|omega_dot/omega^2| = 0.025 (COM, harmonic ramp-down) and 0.015 (around the sign change of the quadratic coefficient, no mode label)
  substituting ordinary frequency changes these by 2 pi = 6.2832 and destroys the numbers
splitting chi = d_ddot_CP/(d_CP omega_CP^2), chi < 1 adiabatic; tau_CP = pi/omega_CP = 2.834 us at trap A
adiabatic suppression exp[c^2(1 - 1/chi)] with c UNDEFINED in the source; a reconstruction gives c ~ 0.93
  T =    60 us at chi(60 us) = 1: chi = 1.0000, suppression exp[0.93^2(1 - 1/chi)] = 1.000e+00
  T =   200 us at chi(60 us) = 1: chi = 0.0900, suppression exp[0.93^2(1 - 1/chi)] = 1.592e-04
  T =   500 us at chi(60 us) = 1: chi = 0.0144, suppression exp[0.93^2(1 - 1/chi)] = 1.953e-26
  -> the adiabatic branch is T^-2 times a GAUSSIAN in T, not an exponential in T

